<macros>
    <token name="@TOOL_VERSION@">0.8.2</token>
    <token name="@VERSION_SUFFIX@">0</token>
    <token name="@PROFILE@">24.1</token>
    <xml name="requirements">
        <requirements>
            <requirement type="package" version="@TOOL_VERSION@">krepp</requirement>
        </requirements>
    </xml>
    <xml name="version_command">
        <version_command>krepp --version 2&gt;&amp;1 | head -n1</version_command>
    </xml>
    <xml name="stdio">
        <stdio>
            <exit_code range="1:"/>
            <exit_code range=":-1"/>
            <regex match="Error:"/>
            <regex match="Exception:"/>
        </stdio>
    </xml>
    <xml name="citations">
        <citations>
            <citation type="doi">10.1186/s13059-026-03999-y</citation>
        </citations>
    </xml>
    <token name="@ATTRIBUTION@">**Attribution**

This Galaxy tool wrapper is based on krepp, a k-mer-based maximum
pseudo-likelihood tool for estimating distances of reads to genomes and
performing genome-wide phylogenetic placement.

krepp is available from
[bioconda](https://anaconda.org/bioconda/krepp) and its source code is
hosted on [GitHub](https://github.com/bo1929/krepp).</token>
    <token name="@THREADS@">--num-threads \${GALAXY_SLOTS:-4}</token>
</macros>
